Z||000004||Fiero_24||06-17-2001||04:33 PM||||Just keep me posted, and send a pic ASAP of the finished ones.  I am sure there are a lot of us patiently waiting to see how they turn out.<P><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||06-19-2001||03:21 AM||||Update:<P>I made 2 pair of vents today.  I picked up a quart of white gelcoat, a whole bunch of paint brushes, and went to work.  The first set turned out ok, but weak in the corners.  The gelcoat formed the corner, but there is some air bubbles in them.  Im giving them to a friend to put on his lumina, and he is going to try and salvage them.  The second set turned out alot better in the corners, I cut the fiberglass to the exact size before I layed it up with resin.  Problem though, for some reason the mold release decided to get ahold of the plaster and peel a thin section out of the middle of the mold.  The plaster was stuck to the gel coat.  So I coated the entire middle of the mold with POR-15.  POR-15 is a rust preventive paint that dries real hard, smooth, glossy and practically indestructable.  Im going to sand it out tommorow, fill the section that is scared, and recoat it with POR-15.  I figured that since the mold release is water based (partall #10) it must of soaked into the plaster, and didnt form a barrier from the gelcoat.  Anyway, im getting this stuff figured out.  If anyone wants the other messed up pair of vents, Ill sell them to ya real cheap! If not, Ill have some good ones ready in a few days.||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadaver||06-19-2001||05:11 PM||||I see you have learned why not to make molds for glass out of plaster.<BR>What release are you using?||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||06-19-2001||05:11 PM||||Are you using cloth or mat?<BR>What weight?||||reg||1
Z||000008||pontiacs4me||06-19-2001||06:23 PM||||Cadaver, Im using partall #10 mold release.  I am using mat fiberglass, Not sure of the weight, pretty thick though.  <BR>I sanded the por-15 today, filled the scars in the mold, and recoated it with por-15.  this stuff dries so hard and indestructable, Ill never have this problem again.  Im going to sand and buff the mold to a nice smooth orangepeel free surface, and Ill be ready to give it another try.||||reg||1
